cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "agenttape: deterministic record and replay for AI agents"
abstract: >-
  agenttape records AI agent runs to local, append-only, hash-chained tapes and
  replays them offline. Replaying a tape re-runs the agent's own logic while
  every external answer -- model responses, tool results, clock reads, random
  draws -- is served from the recording, with no live calls and no side effects.
  Divergence from the recording halts with a diff instead of being silently
  tolerated. The library is pure Python with no runtime dependencies and is
  intended to be embedded in an agent runtime rather than invoked as a tool.
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-17"
keywords:
  - ai agents
  - llm
  - deterministic replay
  - record and replay
  - reproducibility
  - debugging
  - rollback
  - observability
authors:
